Z||000004||loafer87gt||04-22-2000||10:19 PM||||My 87GT weighed in at 2957 last summer. That was with my two sub boxes and 4 10" sub woofers, and amps. By the way, this is a bit off topic, but did you guys know that those new Civic SIRs weigh in at 3000 lbs!?!! My brothers old 92 Civic SI was a little over 2400 lbs, so I don't know where the extra weight came from. He just took a 160 HP model out for a test drive and he said it felt slower than his 125 HP car. I guess weight makes a big difference in a cars performance. In Hot Rod magazine they said that for every 100 lbs you trim off your car it is equivalent to a 10 HP gain. ||||reg||1
