Z||000011||Patrick's Dad||04-24-2000||11:15 AM||||Loafer: That extra weight is mostly safety equipment. Steel door beams, dual airbags, etc., plus the normal bloat that happens to a car as it ages. The bean counters say to themselves, "These are the most popular options, so, if we make them standard, their cost per unit (higher volume of purchase and labor) lowers, and more cars will be made with fewer "options," thereby reducing production costs overall. I can't imagine what the last 280ZX weighed in at before the 300's came out. Alas, this probably would have happened to our poor Fiero....||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||04-24-2000||12:26 PM||||According to the Fiero book (by HPBooks) the weight for a base coupe is 2480 85GT/86,87SE is 2531 and 86/87GT is 2708. This is factory measured curb weight. Add about 88 lbs for a full tank of gas. The book does not list weights for 88 Fiero's||||reg||1
